---
layout: layouts/base.njk
description: Arin is a local daemon that draws on your screen. Any AI can point, highlight, and explain over MCP or a small JSON protocol. It draws. It never clicks.
---

<section class="relative mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 pb-16 pt-36 lg:pt-44">
  <div class="grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <p class="mb-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-white/10 bg-white/5 px-3.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium tracking-wide text-secondary-soft">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-secondary"></span>
        Local daemon for macOS
      </p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold leading-[1.05] tracking-tight text-frost sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
        An annotation layer any agent can
        <span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-primary-soft via-secondary-soft to-tertiary-soft bg-clip-text text-transparent">draw on</span>.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-measure-tight text-lg leading-relaxed text-mist">
        Arin draws on your screen. Agents point at things, highlight regions, and write
        explanations over MCP or a small JSON protocol. It draws. It never clicks.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
        <a href="/docs/quickstart/" class="rounded-xl bg-primary px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-abyss shadow-lg shadow-primary/25 transition hover:bg-primary-soft">
          Get started
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/" class="glass rounded-xl px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-frost transition hover:border-white/20">
          Read the docs
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="glass mt-8 inline-flex max-w-full items-center gap-3 rounded-xl px-4 py-3 font-mono text-sm text-secondary-soft">
        <span class="select-none text-mist">$</span>
        <code class="break-words">brew install anistark/tools/arin</code>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="glass glass-edge min-w-0 rounded-3xl p-3 sm:p-4">
      {% include "partials/hero-canvas.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-measure-tight text-center" data-reveal>
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-frost sm:text-4xl">It draws. It never clicks.</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-mist">
      Arin never synthesises input. No clicks, no keystrokes, no scrolling. That boundary
      is the point.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
    <div class="glass glass-edge rounded-2xl p-6" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 0">
      <div class="mb-4 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-primary/15 text-primary-soft">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 19c-4 0-7-3-7-7s3-7 7-7 7 3 7 7"/><path d="m15 15 6 6"/><path d="M12 9v0M12 12v0"/></svg>
      </div>
      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-frost">Safe to leave running</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist">
        A tool that can only render pixels cannot act on your behalf. Agents that need to
        click should compose Arin with a separate actuator.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="glass glass-edge rounded-2xl p-6" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 1">
      <div class="mb-4 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-secondary/15 text-secondary-soft">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="10" rx="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg>
      </div>
      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-frost">No Accessibility permission</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist">
        Screen Recording is the only permission Arin asks for, and frames are compared in
        memory rather than written or sent anywhere.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="glass glass-edge rounded-2xl p-6" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 2">
      <div class="mb-4 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-tertiary/15 text-tertiary-soft">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m18 16 4-4-4-4"/><path d="m6 8-4 4 4 4"/><path d="m14.5 4-5 16"/></svg>
      </div>
      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-frost">Auditable in an afternoon</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist">
        Arin holds no model and makes no decisions. The intelligence is your agent. Arin
        is the chalk.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-measure-tight text-center" data-reveal>
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-frost sm:text-4xl">From tool call to pixels</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-mist">
      One round trip, entirely on your machine.
    </p>
  </div>
  <ol class="relative mx-auto mt-14 grid max-w-5xl gap-10 lg:grid-cols-4 lg:gap-6">
    <div class="pointer-events-none absolute left-6 top-0 h-full w-px bg-gradient-to-b from-primary/60 via-secondary/40 to-tertiary/60 lg:left-0 lg:top-6 lg:h-px lg:w-full lg:bg-gradient-to-r" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <li class="relative pl-16 lg:pl-0 lg:pt-16" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 0">
      <span class="absolute left-0 top-0 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-primary/40 bg-abyss font-mono text-sm text-primary-soft shadow-lg shadow-primary/20">01</span>
      <h3 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-frost">Your agent decides</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist">A model wants to show you something and calls a tool instead of describing a location in prose.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="relative pl-16 lg:pl-0 lg:pt-16" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 1">
      <span class="absolute left-0 top-0 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-secondary/40 bg-abyss font-mono text-sm text-secondary-soft shadow-lg shadow-secondary/20">02</span>
      <h3 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-frost">Arin places it</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist">Coordinates, a named anchor, or a described target through a resolver all land on the right display.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="relative pl-16 lg:pl-0 lg:pt-16" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 2">
      <span class="absolute left-0 top-0 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-tertiary/40 bg-abyss font-mono text-sm text-tertiary-soft shadow-lg shadow-tertiary/20">03</span>
      <h3 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-frost">The mark renders</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist">Arin picks a colour that stays visible against whatever is underneath and draws above every window.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="relative pl-16 lg:pl-0 lg:pt-16" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 3">
      <span class="absolute left-0 top-0 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-primary/40 bg-abyss font-mono text-sm text-primary-soft shadow-lg shadow-primary/20">04</span>
      <h3 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-frost">It cleans up</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist">Marks expire on TTL, leave with their session, and are invalidated the moment content scrolls away.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-measure-tight text-center" data-reveal>
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-frost sm:text-4xl">Two ways in, three ways to drive</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-mist">
      One binary is the daemon, the MCP server, and the command line tool. However you
      install it and whatever talks to it, that is the same build.
    </p>
  </div>

  {#
    A bento rather than a row of equal cards, because these are not equal. Installing is a
    thing you do once and driving is a thing you do every day, and MCP is the one most
    people arrive for, so it is the one that gets the room. The eyebrow on each card says
    which of the two it is.
  #}
  <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-6">
    {# The hero of the bento: two columns wide and two rows tall, because pointing at a
       codebase while an agent explains it is the thing Arin is for. #}
    <div class="reveal-card glass glass-edge relative flex flex-col rounded-2xl p-6 lg:col-span-4 lg:row-span-2" data-reveal data-reveal-card style="--reveal-delay: 0">
      <span class="reveal-card__glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="reveal-card__field" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <div class="relative z-10 flex flex-1 flex-col">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-primary-soft/70">Drive</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-frost">From an agent</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist">
          An agent explaining an article can circle each section as it talks about it. A
          reviewer can point at the exact line it means. Four tools do all of it, named
          after what the agent is trying to do rather than after the message underneath,
          so a model reaches for the right one without being told.
        </p>

        {# The vocabulary, which used to be a section of its own further down the page. It
           belongs here: these are the four tools the sentence above is counting, so the
           list and the claim cannot drift apart. `draw` is not among them, because MCP does
           not expose it. It is a protocol message, and it is named on the shell card. #}
        <div class="mt-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="group/tool rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-deep/50 p-4">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 120 44" class="h-11 w-full" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="60" cy="22" r="14" fill="#4C8DFF" opacity="0.15" class="transition-transform duration-500 group-hover/tool:scale-125" style="transform-origin: center"/>
              <circle cx="60" cy="22" r="7" fill="#4C8DFF" opacity="0.45"/>
              <circle cx="60" cy="22" r="3" fill="#A9DCFF"/>
            </svg>
            <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-sm text-primary-soft">point_at</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed text-mist">Puts the orb on a position, with an optional caption.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="group/tool rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-deep/50 p-4">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 120 44" class="h-11 w-full" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="30" y="8" width="60" height="28" rx="7" stroke="#3DDC97" stroke-width="2" fill="#3DDC97" fill-opacity="0.08" class="transition-transform duration-500 group-hover/tool:scale-105" style="transform-origin: center"/>
              <rect x="40" y="18" width="34" height="3.5" rx="1.75" fill="#3DDC97" opacity="0.35"/>
              <rect x="40" y="26" width="22" height="3.5" rx="1.75" fill="#3DDC97" opacity="0.2"/>
            </svg>
            <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-sm text-secondary-soft">highlight</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed text-mist">Frames a region of the screen so it stands out.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="group/tool rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-deep/50 p-4">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 120 44" class="h-11 w-full" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="34" y="4" width="52" height="26" rx="6" stroke="#A78BFA" stroke-opacity="0.6" fill="#0A1020"/>
              <rect x="42" y="12" width="36" height="3.5" rx="1.75" fill="#C9B8FF" opacity="0.7"/>
              <rect x="42" y="20" width="24" height="3.5" rx="1.75" fill="#C9B8FF" opacity="0.4"/>
              <path d="M54 30 L48 38" stroke="#A78BFA" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" class="transition-transform duration-500 group-hover/tool:translate-y-0.5"/>
            </svg>
            <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-sm text-tertiary-soft">annotate</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed text-mist">Writes a short explanation next to the thing it explains.</p>
          </div>

          {# Neutral on purpose. The other three put something on the screen and this one
             takes it away, so it does not get a mark colour. #}
          <div class="group/tool rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-deep/50 p-4">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 120 44" class="h-11 w-full" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="34" cy="22" r="7" fill="#C3CADB" opacity="0.5" class="transition-opacity duration-500 group-hover/tool:opacity-20"/>
              <circle cx="56" cy="22" r="5" fill="#C3CADB" opacity="0.3" class="transition-opacity duration-500 group-hover/tool:opacity-10"/>
              <circle cx="74" cy="22" r="3.5" fill="#C3CADB" opacity="0.18" class="transition-opacity duration-500 group-hover/tool:opacity-0"/>
              <circle cx="88" cy="22" r="2" fill="#C3CADB" opacity="0.1" class="transition-opacity duration-500 group-hover/tool:opacity-0"/>
            </svg>
            <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-sm text-fog">clear</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed text-mist">Removes one mark, or every mark the agent drew.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <pre class="mt-6 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-deep/80 p-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-fog"><code><span class="text-mist"># Claude Code, one line</span>
claude mcp add arin -- arin mcp</code></pre>
        <a href="/docs/mcp/" class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-primary-soft transition hover:text-frost">MCP docs &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-card glass glass-edge relative flex flex-col rounded-2xl p-6 lg:col-span-2" data-reveal data-reveal-card style="--reveal-delay: 1">
      <span class="reveal-card__glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="reveal-card__field" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <div class="group relative z-10 flex flex-1 flex-col">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-fog/60">Install</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-frost">Homebrew</h3>

        <svg viewBox="0 0 120 44" class="mt-4 h-11 w-full" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M46 12 h28 a6 6 0 0 1 6 6 v14 a6 6 0 0 1 -6 6 h-28 a6 6 0 0 1 -6 -6 v-14 a6 6 0 0 1 6 -6 z" stroke="#C3CADB" stroke-opacity="0.45" fill="#0A1020"/>
          <path d="M40 20 h40" stroke="#C3CADB" stroke-opacity="0.3"/>
          <path d="M60 4 v8" stroke="#8FB8FF" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" class="transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:translate-y-1"/>
          <path d="M56 8 l4 4 l4 -4" stroke="#8FB8FF" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:translate-y-1"/>
        </svg>

        <p class="mt-4 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist">
          Compiles where it runs, so nothing is ever quarantined and Gatekeeper never
          engages.
        </p>
        <pre class="mt-4 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-deep/80 p-3 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-fog"><code>brew install anistark/tools/arin</code></pre>
        <a href="/docs/install/" class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-primary-soft transition hover:text-frost">Install docs &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-card glass glass-edge relative flex flex-col rounded-2xl p-6 lg:col-span-2" data-reveal data-reveal-card style="--reveal-delay: 2">
      <span class="reveal-card__glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="reveal-card__field" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <div class="group relative z-10 flex flex-1 flex-col">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-fog/60">Install</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-frost">Nix</h3>

        <svg viewBox="0 0 120 44" class="mt-4 h-11 w-full" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <g stroke="#8FB8FF" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" class="transition-transform duration-700 group-hover:rotate-60" style="transform-origin: 60px 22px">
            <path d="M60 6 v32" stroke-opacity="0.75"/>
            <path d="M46 14 l28 16" stroke-opacity="0.5"/>
            <path d="M74 14 l-28 16" stroke-opacity="0.5"/>
          </g>
          <circle cx="60" cy="22" r="3" fill="#A9DCFF"/>
        </svg>

        <p class="mt-4 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist">
          A flake for both Macs, with a nix-darwin module that puts the daemon's options
          under version control.
        </p>
        <pre class="mt-4 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-deep/80 p-3 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-fog"><code>nix run github:anistark/arin -- -d</code></pre>
        <a href="/docs/nix/" class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-primary-soft transition hover:text-frost">Nix docs &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-card glass glass-edge relative flex flex-col rounded-2xl p-6 lg:col-span-3" data-reveal data-reveal-card style="--reveal-delay: 3">
      <span class="reveal-card__glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="reveal-card__field" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <div class="group relative z-10 flex flex-1 flex-col">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-secondary-soft/70">Drive</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-frost">From a shell</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist">
          The same protocol an agent speaks, which makes it the quickest way to see what a
          mark actually looks like. It reaches one more than MCP does: <code class="font-mono text-secondary-soft">draw</code>,
          for freehand circles, arrows and underlines.
        </p>
        <pre class="mt-4 flex-1 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-deep/80 p-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-fog"><code><span class="text-secondary-soft">$</span> arin point --at top-right --label "the close button"</code></pre>
        <a href="/docs/cli/" class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-secondary-soft transition hover:text-frost">CLI docs &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-card glass glass-edge relative flex flex-col rounded-2xl p-6 lg:col-span-3" data-reveal data-reveal-card style="--reveal-delay: 4">
      <span class="reveal-card__glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="reveal-card__field" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <div class="group relative z-10 flex flex-1 flex-col">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-tertiary-soft/70">Drive</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-frost">From anything</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist">
          Newline-delimited JSON over a Unix socket. No client library, and no listening
          port to find.
        </p>
        <pre class="mt-4 flex-1 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-deep/80 p-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-fog"><code>{"v":"0.1","type":"point","x":412,"y":88,"label":"Save"}</code></pre>
        <a href="/docs/protocol/" class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-tertiary-soft transition hover:text-frost">Protocol docs &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16">
  <div class="glass glass-edge rounded-3xl px-8 py-12 text-center sm:px-16" data-reveal>
    <img src="/assets/brand/logo.png" alt="" class="mx-auto mb-6 h-16 w-16">
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-frost">Give your agent some chalk</h2>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-measure-tight text-mist">
      One brew install away. Needs macOS 14 or newer.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4">
      <a href="/docs/install/" class="rounded-xl bg-primary px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-abyss shadow-lg shadow-primary/25 transition hover:bg-primary-soft">
        Install Arin
      </a>
      <a href="{{ site.repo }}" class="glass rounded-xl px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-frost transition hover:border-white/20">
        Star on GitHub
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
